contentText:
Grammy-nominated singer Duncan Sheik is hospitalized in critical condition while battling an undisclosed ailment, according to a statement posted by his family on Instagram on Wednesday (Sept. 16).

At press time it was unknown why Sheik was in the hospital, but on Sept. 6 the 56-year-old singer posted a selfie on Instagram, reporting, &#8220;Sorry for the selfies. But I&#8217;m still bored in hospital. Do you like (good) magazines?&#8221; It appears as if &#8220;Barely Breathing&#8221; singer has been in a hospital for nearly a month judging by an Aug. 20 post of Sheik in a medical gown with the caption, &#8220;I would prefer to be home making music. But a bit of reflection is not too bad … boring hospital stays have their benefits (outside the obvious.)&#8221;

Subsequent posts from Aug. 23 and appeared to show the view from inside a hospital room of a sunrise and, on Aug. 26, a TV mounted on a wall . On Sept. 7 he posted yet another selfie, writing, &#8220; out of here in 60 hours .&#8221;

A number of fellow musicians sent their best wishes in comments on Wednesday&#8217;s post, including Lisa Loeb (&#8220;Sending love&#8221;), Matt Nathanson (&#8220;sending big love&#8221;), Broadway star Tyce Green (&#8220;Buddy you&#8217;ve got this. You&#8217;ve got this. !!!!!&#8221;) and Lizzo.

At press time a spokesperson for Sheik could not be reached for comment on his condition, but the latest news comes just before the opening of the manga novel adaptation Memoirs of Amorous Gentleman , a musical for which Sheik wrote the score; the off-Broadway show is slated to open on Oct. 15 at the Night Egg at the Culture Club.

Sheik is best known for his Grammy-nominated 1996 Billboard Hot 100 No. 16 debut single, &#8220;Barely Breathing,&#8221; as well as his Tony Award for best original score and best orchestration for the 2006 coming-of-age rock musical Spring Awakening . In the years since, he wrote the music for Alice By Heart , the 2013 musical adaptation of the Bret Easton Ellis horror novel American Psycho as well as the 2013 musical adaptation of Because of Winn-Dixie . His most recent album was 2022&#8217;s Claptrap .
